{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_0","type":"agent_message","text":"{\"id\":\"R-90:16\",\"status\":\"reading\",\"finding\":\"The poor person “with dust” in 90:16 makes the steep path materially social; the next verse places mutual patience and mercy within that same path, alongside the focus ayah’s deeds and patience.\",\"evidence\":[{\"ref\":\"90:16\",\"ar\":\"أَوْ مِسْكِينًۭا ذَا مَتْرَبَةٍۢ\"},{\"ref\":\"90:17\",\"ar\":\"ثُمَّ كَانَ مِنَ ٱلَّذِينَ ءَامَنُوا۟ وَتَوَاصَوْا۟ بِٱلصَّبْرِ وَتَوَاصَوْا۟ بِٱلْمَرْحَمَةِ\"},{\"ref\":\"103:3\",\"ar\":\"وَعَمِلُوا۟ ٱلصَّٰلِحَٰتِ وَتَوَاصَوْا۟ بِٱلْحَقِّ وَتَوَاصَوْا۟ بِٱلصَّبْرِ\"}],\"activation\":\"The focus joins righteous deeds to mutual counsel in patience; 90:16–17 places care for the poor immediately before a community marked by mutual patience and mercy.\",\"limits\":\"The passage does not identify this particular act of care as the full meaning of ٱلصَّٰلِحَٰتِ, and its second counsel is mercy rather than truth.\",\"support\":\"strong\",\"relevance\":\"high\"}\n{\"id\":\"R-90:17\",\"status\":\"reading\",\"finding\":\"The close parallel in faith and mutual counsel of patience presents the focus ayah’s final clauses as communal practices; 90:17 pairs patience with mercy, while 103:3 pairs it with truth.\",\"evidence\":[{\"ref\":\"90:17\",\"ar\":\"ءَامَنُوا۟ وَتَوَاصَوْا۟ بِٱلصَّبْرِ وَتَوَاصَوْا۟ بِٱلْمَرْحَمَةِ\"},{\"ref\":\"103:3\",\"ar\":\"ءَامَنُوا۟ وَعَمِلُوا۟ ٱلصَّٰلِحَٰتِ وَتَوَاصَوْا۟ بِٱلْحَقِّ وَتَوَاصَوْا۟ بِٱلصَّبْرِ\"}],\"activation\":\"Both passages name believers and repeat تَوَاصَوْا۟ بِٱلصَّبْرِ; the focus adds righteous deeds and mutual counsel in truth.\",\"limits\":\"The parallel does not make ٱلْمَرْحَمَةِ and ٱلْحَقِّ interchangeable, and 90:17’s ثُمَّ gives its clauses a sequence absent from the focus.\",\"support\":\"strong\",\"relevance\":\"high\"}\n{\"id\":\"R-90:19\",\"status\":\"reading\",\"finding\":\"Surah 90 sets believers who counsel patience and mercy among the people of the right against deniers identified as the people of the left; this gives the focus ayah’s excepted group a counterpart defined by denial.\",\"evidence\":[{\"ref\":\"90:18\",\"ar\":\"أُو۟لَٰٓئِكَ أَصْحَٰبُ ٱلْمَيْمَنَةِ\"},{\"ref\":\"90:19\",\"ar\":\"وَٱلَّذِينَ كَفَرُوا۟ بِـَٔايَٰتِنَا هُمْ أَصْحَٰبُ ٱلْمَشْـَٔمَةِ\"},{\"ref\":\"103:3\",\"ar\":\"إِلَّا ٱلَّذِينَ ءَامَنُوا۟ وَعَمِلُوا۟ ٱلصَّٰلِحَٰتِ وَتَوَاصَوْا۟ بِٱلْحَقِّ وَتَوَاصَوْا۟ بِٱلصَّبْرِ\"}],\"activation\":\"The focus defines its exception through faith and reciprocal practices, while 90:19 defines the opposing group by rejecting signs.\",\"limits\":\"The two surahs do not state that their group labels or outcomes are identical.\",\"support\":\"medium\",\"relevance\":\"high\"}\n{\"id\":\"R-90:20\",\"status\":\"note\",\"finding\":\"The fire closing Surah 90 gives a severe outcome to its deniers, sharpening the stakes of the group contrast around 90:17 and the focus ayah’s escape from loss.\",\"evidence\":[{\"ref\":\"90:19\",\"ar\":\"وَٱلَّذِينَ كَفَرُوا۟ بِـَٔايَٰتِنَا هُمْ أَصْحَٰبُ ٱلْمَشْـَٔمَةِ\"},{\"ref\":\"90:20\",\"ar\":\"عَلَيْهِمْ نَارٌۭ مُّؤْصَدَةٌۢ\"},{\"ref\":\"103:2\",\"ar\":\"إِنَّ ٱلْإِنسَٰنَ لَفِى خُسْرٍ\"}],\"activation\":\"Both passages place a negative human outcome beside a description of those who escape or oppose it.\",\"limits\":\"The focus does not name fire or specify the fate of those outside its exception.\",\"support\":\"strong\",\"relevance\":\"medium\"}\n{\"id\":\"R-91:10\",\"status\":\"reading\",\"finding\":\"The paired claim that the soul’s purifier succeeds and its corrupter fails offers a distinct success-and-failure frame for the focus ayah’s exception to human loss.\",\"evidence\":[{\"ref\":\"91:9\",\"ar\":\"قَدْ أَفْلَحَ مَن زَكَّىٰهَا\"},{\"ref\":\"91:10\",\"ar\":\"وَقَدْ خَابَ مَن دَسَّىٰهَا\"},{\"ref\":\"103:2\",\"ar\":\"إِنَّ ٱلْإِنسَٰنَ لَفِى خُسْرٍ\"},{\"ref\":\"103:3\",\"ar\":\"إِلَّا ٱلَّذِينَ ءَامَنُوا۟ وَعَمِلُوا۟ ٱلصَّٰلِحَٰتِ\"}],\"activation\":\"The focus moves from a general human loss to an excepted group; 91:9–10 likewise contrasts success with failure through opposed human acts.\",\"limits\":\"The passages use different terms and do not equate تزكية with the focus ayah’s four conditions.\",\"support\":\"medium\",\"relevance\":\"high\"}\n{\"id\":\"R-92:5\",\"status\":\"reading\",\"finding\":\"Surah 92 presents giving and taqwa followed by affirming al-ḥusnā as a route parallel in shape to the focus ayah’s faith, deeds, and truth; the focus uniquely makes its counsel reciprocal.\",\"evidence\":[{\"ref\":\"92:5\",\"ar\":\"فَأَمَّا مَنْ أَعْطَىٰ وَٱتَّقَىٰ\"},{\"ref\":\"92:6\",\"ar\":\"وَصَدَّقَ بِٱلْحُسْنَىٰ\"},{\"ref\":\"103:3\",\"ar\":\"ءَامَنُوا۟ وَعَمِلُوا۟ ٱلصَّٰلِحَٰتِ وَتَوَاصَوْا۟ بِٱلْحَقِّ\"}],\"activation\":\"Both sequences coordinate concrete action with an affirmation, though 92:5–6 describes one person and the focus ayah a plural group.\",\"limits\":\"The excerpt does not establish that ٱلْحُسْنَىٰ means ٱلْحَقِّ or that giving is the whole sense of ٱلصَّٰلِحَٰتِ.\",\"support\":\"medium\",\"relevance\":\"high\"}\n{\"id\":\"R-94:5\",\"status\":\"open\",\"finding\":\"The repeated pairing of hardship with ease could supply a pressure setting for the focus ayah’s counsel of patience.\",\"evidence\":[{\"ref\":\"94:5\",\"ar\":\"فَإِنَّ مَعَ ٱلْعُسْرِ يُسْرًا\"},{\"ref\":\"94:6\",\"ar\":\"إِنَّ مَعَ ٱلْعُسْرِ يُسْرًۭا\"},{\"ref\":\"103:3\",\"ar\":\"وَتَوَاصَوْا۟ بِٱلصَّبْرِ\"}],\"missing\":\"The focus names patience but no hardship; another explicit Qur’anic link between ṣabr and ʿusr could establish whether this pairing specifies the pressure under which its counsel operates.\",\"support\":\"medium\",\"relevance\":\"high\"}\n{\"id\":\"R-94:7\",\"status\":\"open\",\"finding\":\"The command to strive after becoming free could suggest that the focus ayah’s practices continue across changing tasks rather than ending with a completed effort.\",\"evidence\":[{\"ref\":\"94:7\",\"ar\":\"فَإِذَا فَرَغْتَ فَٱنصَبْ\"},{\"ref\":\"94:8\",\"ar\":\"وَإِلَىٰ رَبِّكَ فَٱرْغَب\"},{\"ref\":\"103:3\",\"ar\":\"وَعَمِلُوا۟ ٱلصَّٰلِحَٰتِ وَتَوَاصَوْا۟ بِٱلْحَقِّ\"}],\"missing\":\"The focus contains no marker of completion or renewed striving, and 94:7 addresses one person rather than mutual counsel; a further passage connecting striving after completion to communal exhortation could establish the link.\",\"support\":\"weak\",\"relevance\":\"medium\"}\n{\"id\":\"R-95:1\",\"status\":\"none\",\"code\":\"no-link\"}\n{\"id\":\"R-95:3\",\"status\":\"open\",\"finding\":\"The focus verb ءَامَنُوا۟ and the secure-city description ٱلْبَلَدِ ٱلْأَمِينِ share the أمن root, raising a possible security resonance for faith.\",\"evidence\":[{\"ref\":\"95:3\",\"ar\":\"وَهَٰذَا ٱلْبَلَدِ ٱلْأَمِينِ\"},{\"ref\":\"103:3\",\"ar\":\"إِلَّا ٱلَّذِينَ ءَامَنُوا۟\"}],\"missing\":\"The shared root alone does not establish that the city’s safety sense colors ءَامَنُوا۟ here; dictionary evidence or another Qur’anic usage that bridges security and belief could decide whether this changes the focus reading.\",\"support\":\"medium\",\"relevance\":\"high\"}\n{\"id\":\"R-95:4\",\"status\":\"reading\",\"finding\":\"Surah 95 moves from humanity’s creation in best form to a downward return, then excepts believers who act righteously; this supplies a human-condition-and-exception parallel to the focus ayah’s universal loss and named exit.\",\"evidence\":[{\"ref\":\"95:4\",\"ar\":\"لَقَدْ خَلَقْنَا ٱلْإِنسَٰنَ فِىٓ أَحْسَنِ تَقْوِيمٍۢ\"},{\"ref\":\"95:5\",\"ar\":\"ثُمَّ رَدَدْنَٰهُ أَسْفَلَ سَٰفِلِينَ\"},{\"ref\":\"95:6\",\"ar\":\"إِلَّا ٱلَّذِينَ ءَامَنُوا۟ وَعَمِلُوا۟ ٱلصَّٰلِحَٰتِ\"},{\"ref\":\"103:3\",\"ar\":\"إِلَّا ٱلَّذِينَ ءَامَنُوا۟ وَعَمِلُوا۟ ٱلصَّٰلِحَٰتِ\"}],\"activation\":\"The focus’s exception follows the verdict that humanity is in loss, while Surah 95’s exception follows its account of humanity’s descent.\",\"limits\":\"The surahs use different descriptions of the human condition and different consequences; this parallel does not define loss as a descent to the lowest state.\",\"support\":\"strong\",\"relevance\":\"high\"}\n{\"id\":\"R-95:6\",\"status\":\"reading\",\"finding\":\"The repeated exception formula for faith and righteous deeds makes the focus ayah’s addition stand out: it attaches reciprocal counsel of truth and patience to a familiar membership description.\",\"evidence\":[{\"ref\":\"95:6\",\"ar\":\"إِلَّا ٱلَّذِينَ ءَامَنُوا۟ وَعَمِلُوا۟ ٱلصَّٰلِحَٰتِ فَلَهُمْ أَجْرٌ غَيْرُ مَمْنُونٍۢ\"},{\"ref\":\"103:3\",\"ar\":\"إِلَّا ٱلَّذِينَ ءَامَنُوا۟ وَعَمِلُوا۟ ٱلصَّٰلِحَٰتِ وَتَوَاصَوْا۟ بِٱلْحَقِّ وَتَوَاصَوْا۟ بِٱلصَّبْرِ\"}],\"activation\":\"The wording through ٱلصَّٰلِحَٰتِ is shared, and the focus continues with two coordinated mutual-charge clauses.\",\"limits\":\"Surah 95 names an unending reward, whereas the focus ayah does not state that consequence.\",\"support\":\"strong\",\"relevance\":\"high\"}\n{\"id\":\"R-95:8\",\"status\":\"none\",\"code\":\"no-link\"}\n{\"id\":\"R-98:7\",\"status\":\"reading\",\"finding\":\"Surah 98 places the same faith-and-righteous-deeds group opposite its deniers and calls that group the best of creation; this frames the focus’s exception as a communal identity, while the focus adds reciprocal obligations.\",\"evidence\":[{\"ref\":\"98:6\",\"ar\":\"إِنَّ ٱلَّذِينَ كَفَرُوا۟ مِنْ أَهْلِ ٱلْكِتَٰبِ وَٱلْمُشْرِكِينَ\"},{\"ref\":\"98:7\",\"ar\":\"إِنَّ ٱلَّذِينَ ءَامَنُوا۟ وَعَمِلُوا۟ ٱلصَّٰلِحَٰتِ أُو۟لَٰٓئِكَ هُمْ خَيْرُ ٱلْبَرِيَّةِ\"},{\"ref\":\"103:3\",\"ar\":\"ءَامَنُوا۟ وَعَمِلُوا۟ ٱلصَّٰلِحَٰتِ وَتَوَاصَوْا۟ بِٱلْحَقِّ\"}],\"activation\":\"The matching faith-and-deeds formula appears in both verses, and Surah 98 explicitly sets its group against deniers.\",\"limits\":\"The focus does not use خَيْرُ ٱلْبَرِيَّةِ or name the contrasting group in the way 98:6–7 does.\",\"support\":\"strong\",\"relevance\":\"high\"}\n{\"id\":\"R-99:1\",\"status\":\"none\",\"code\":\"no-link\"}\n{\"id\":\"R-99:2\",\"status\":\"none\",\"code\":\"no-link\"}\n{\"id\":\"R-99:3\",\"status\":\"none\",\"code\":\"no-link\"}\n{\"id\":\"R-99:5\",\"status\":\"open\",\"finding\":\"The sequence from earth recounting its news to people being shown their deeds could form a witness-and-accountability backdrop for the focus’s good deeds and truth, but the focus names human mutual counsel instead.\",\"evidence\":[{\"ref\":\"99:4\",\"ar\":\"يَوْمَئِذٍۢ تُحَدِّثُ أَخْبَارَهَا\"},{\"ref\":\"99:5\",\"ar\":\"بِأَنَّ رَبَّكَ أَوْحَىٰ لَهَا\"},{\"ref\":\"99:6\",\"ar\":\"يَوْمَئِذٍۢ يَصْدُرُ ٱلنَّاسُ أَشْتَاتًۭا لِّيُرَوْا۟ أَعْمَٰلَهُمْ\"},{\"ref\":\"103:3\",\"ar\":\"وَعَمِلُوا۟ ٱلصَّٰلِحَٰتِ وَتَوَاصَوْا۟ بِٱلْحَقِّ\"}],\"missing\":\"The passage does not identify earth’s news with righteous deeds or with the focus’s counsel of truth; an explicit link between earthly witness and the moral content of those deeds could establish the connection.\",\"support\":\"medium\",\"relevance\":\"medium\"}\n{\"id\":\"R-99:6\",\"status\":\"note\",\"finding\":\"The scene of people dispersed to be shown their deeds supplies an accountability horizon for the focus’s named righteous work.\",\"evidence\":[{\"ref\":\"99:6\",\"ar\":\"يَوْمَئِذٍۢ يَصْدُرُ ٱلنَّاسُ أَشْتَاتًۭا لِّيُرَوْا۟ أَعْمَٰلَهُمْ\"},{\"ref\":\"103:3\",\"ar\":\"وَعَمِلُوا۟ ٱلصَّٰلِحَٰتِ\"}],\"activation\":\"The focus names acts as part of the exception from loss; Surah 99 depicts people being shown their deeds.\",\"limits\":\"Surah 99 does not single out righteous deeds or mutual counsel in this verse.\",\"support\":\"strong\",\"relevance\":\"medium\"}\n{\"id\":\"R-99:7\",\"status\":\"reading\",\"finding\":\"The atom-weight example makes good action count even at the smallest scale, giving ٱلصَّٰلِحَٰتِ in the focus a concrete measure of deed-by-deed accountability.\",\"evidence\":[{\"ref\":\"99:7\",\"ar\":\"فَمَن يَعْمَلْ مِثْقَالَ ذَرَّةٍ خَيْرًۭا يَرَهُۥ\"},{\"ref\":\"103:3\",\"ar\":\"وَعَمِلُوا۟ ٱلصَّٰلِحَٰتِ\"}],\"activation\":\"Both verses foreground work, and 99:7 specifies an extremely small amount of good action.\",\"limits\":\"The focus does not define ٱلصَّٰلِحَٰتِ by weight or explicitly state that each deed will be seen.\",\"support\":\"strong\",\"relevance\":\"medium\"}\n{\"id\":\"R-99:8\",\"status\":\"note\",\"finding\":\"The matching atom-weight statement for evil deeds keeps the focus’s positive exception within a broader reckoning that also exposes harmful action.\",\"evidence\":[{\"ref\":\"99:7\",\"ar\":\"فَمَن يَعْمَلْ مِثْقَالَ ذَرَّةٍ خَيْرًۭا يَرَهُۥ\"},{\"ref\":\"99:8\",\"ar\":\"وَمَن يَعْمَلْ مِثْقَالَ ذَرَّةٍۢ شَرًّۭا يَرَهُۥ\"},{\"ref\":\"103:3\",\"ar\":\"وَعَمِلُوا۟ ٱلصَّٰلِحَٰتِ\"}],\"activation\":\"The focus specifies righteous deeds among its conditions; the paired verses distinguish good from evil while subjecting both to seeing.\",\"limits\":\"The focus does not describe judgment or say that its excepted group is exempt from the wider accounting.\",\"support\":\"strong\",\"relevance\":\"medium\"}\n{\"id\":\"R-103:1\",\"status\":\"reading\",\"finding\":\"The oath by ٱلْعَصْرِ frames the short surah’s claim of universal loss and its exception under a time-word, so the four practices are presented as the route through that frame.\",\"evidence\":[{\"ref\":\"103:1\",\"ar\":\"وَٱلْعَصْرِ\"},{\"ref\":\"103:2\",\"ar\":\"إِنَّ ٱلْإِنسَٰنَ لَفِى خُسْرٍ\"},{\"ref\":\"103:3\",\"ar\":\"إِلَّا ٱلَّذِينَ ءَامَنُوا۟ وَعَمِلُوا۟ ٱلصَّٰلِحَٰتِ وَتَوَاصَوْا۟ بِٱلْحَقِّ وَتَوَاصَوْا۟ بِٱلصَّبْرِ\"}],\"activation\":\"The oath opens the surah, and the focus completes its compact sequence as the stated exception to loss.\",\"limits\":\"The arrangement does not establish that ٱلْعَصْرِ specifically means time’s depletion or specify the duration of the practices.\",\"support\":\"strong\",\"relevance\":\"high\"}\n{\"id\":\"R-103:2\",\"status\":\"none\",\"code\":\"plain\"}\n{\"id\":\"R-106:4\",\"status\":\"reading\",\"finding\":\"The same Form IV أمن verb appears with different directions: God secures Quraysh from fear in 106:4, while the focus names people who believe. This opens a possible resonance between received security and faith.\",\"evidence\":[{\"ref\":\"106:4\",\"ar\":\"وَءَامَنَهُم مِّنْ خَوْفٍۭ\"},{\"ref\":\"103:3\",\"ar\":\"إِلَّا ٱلَّذِينَ ءَامَنُوا۟\"}],\"activation\":\"The shared Form IV verb and root connect communal security from fear with the focus’s description of believers.\",\"limits\":\"The verses do not say that the focus’s believers are responding to Quraysh’s protection or that their faith is specifically security from fear.\",\"support\":\"strong\",\"relevance\":\"high\"}\n{\"id\":\"R-107:1\",\"status\":\"reading\",\"finding\":\"Surah 107 tests denial of الدين through the treatment of an orphan and the failure to urge feeding a poor person; this contrasts with the focus’s believing group and its counsel of truth and patience.\",\"evidence\":[{\"ref\":\"107:1\",\"ar\":\"أَرَءَيْتَ ٱلَّذِى يُكَذِّبُ بِٱلدِّينِ\"},{\"ref\":\"107:2\",\"ar\":\"فَذَٰلِكَ ٱلَّذِى يَدُعُّ ٱلْيَتِيمَ\"},{\"ref\":\"107:3\",\"ar\":\"وَلَا يَحُضُّ عَلَىٰ طَعَامِ ٱلْمِسْكِينِ\"},{\"ref\":\"103:3\",\"ar\":\"إِلَّا ٱلَّذِينَ ءَامَنُوا۟\"}],\"activation\":\"The focus makes faith part of an exception group; Surah 107 links denial to concrete conduct toward vulnerable people.\",\"limits\":\"The focus does not name orphans, the poor, or الدين, and the passages do not explicitly equate denial with being outside the exception.\",\"support\":\"strong\",\"relevance\":\"high\"}\n{\"id\":\"R-107:3\",\"status\":\"reading\",\"finding\":\"The failure to urge feeding the poor is a pointed negative counterpart to mutual counsel: 107:3 describes no urging, while 103:3 repeats تَوَاصَوْا۟ for truth and patience.\",\"evidence\":[{\"ref\":\"107:3\",\"ar\":\"وَلَا يَحُضُّ عَلَىٰ طَعَامِ ٱلْمِسْكِينِ\"},{\"ref\":\"103:3\",\"ar\":\"وَتَوَاصَوْا۟ بِٱلْحَقِّ وَتَوَاصَوْا۟ بِٱلصَّبْرِ\"}],\"activation\":\"The focus repeats a reciprocal exhortation verb; 107:3 describes a person who does not urge a social good.\",\"limits\":\"The verses use different verbs and the focus does not specify feeding the poor as the content of its counsel.\",\"support\":\"strong\",\"relevance\":\"high\"}\n{\"id\":\"R-f-حقق-صلح-عمل\",\"status\":\"reading\",\"finding\":\"In 4:122, the same faith-and-righteous-deeds formula is followed by God’s promise described as ḥaqq; the focus instead places al-ḥaqq among the obligations believers counsel one another to uphold.\",\"evidence\":[{\"ref\":\"4:122\",\"ar\":\"وَٱلَّذِينَ ءَامَنُوا۟ وَعَمِلُوا۟ ٱلصَّٰلِحَٰتِ\"},{\"ref\":\"4:122\",\"ar\":\"وَعْدَ ٱللَّهِ حَقًّۭا\"},{\"ref\":\"103:3\",\"ar\":\"وَتَوَاصَوْا۟ بِٱلْحَقِّ\"}],\"activation\":\"The shared deeds formula and the root ح ق ق occur in both passages, but in distinct grammatical roles.\",\"limits\":\"The promise called ḥaqq in 4:122 is not the same construction as truth serving as the focus’s counsel payload.\",\"support\":\"strong\",\"relevance\":\"high\"}\n{\"id\":\"R-f-صلح-عمل\",\"status\":\"reading\",\"finding\":\"The recurring formula in 2:25 and 4:173 identifies believers through righteous deeds, often alongside reward; the focus retains that formula and expands it with two reciprocal duties.\",\"evidence\":[{\"ref\":\"2:25\",\"ar\":\"ٱلَّذِينَ ءَامَنُوا۟ وَعَمِلُوا۟ ٱلصَّٰلِحَٰتِ\"},{\"ref\":\"4:173\",\"ar\":\"فَأَمَّا ٱلَّذِينَ ءَامَنُوا۟ وَعَمِلُوا۟ ٱلصَّٰلِحَٰتِ\"},{\"ref\":\"103:3\",\"ar\":\"إِلَّا ٱلَّذِينَ ءَامَنُوا۟ وَعَمِلُوا۟ ٱلصَّٰلِحَٰتِ وَتَوَاصَوْا۟ بِٱلْحَقِّ وَتَوَاصَوْا۟ بِٱلصَّبْرِ\"}],\"activation\":\"The faith-and-deeds wording recurs exactly, and the focus continues past it with reciprocal counsel.\",\"limits\":\"These examples do not establish that every occurrence of the formula has a reward setting or enumerate all deeds meant by ٱلصَّٰلِحَٰتِ.\",\"support\":\"strong\",\"relevance\":\"high\"}\n{\"id\":\"R-f-حقق-عمل\",\"status\":\"open\",\"finding\":\"In 7:43, messengers’ truth and deeds tied to inheriting the Garden appear in one scene; the focus places right or truth and righteous work among a group’s practices, but with different roles.\",\"evidence\":[{\"ref\":\"7:43\",\"ar\":\"لَقَدْ جَآءَتْ رُسُلُ رَبِّنَا بِٱلْحَقِّ\"},{\"ref\":\"7:43\",\"ar\":\"ٱلْجَنَّةُ أُورِثْتُمُوهَا بِمَا كُنتُمْ تَعْمَلُونَ\"},{\"ref\":\"103:3\",\"ar\":\"وَعَمِلُوا۟ ٱلصَّٰلِحَٰتِ وَتَوَاصَوْا۟ بِٱلْحَقِّ\"}],\"missing\":\"The shared roots do not establish that truth as the focus’s counsel content has the same function as messengers bringing truth; another parallel that joins truth-counsel to deeds could clarify the connection.\",\"support\":\"medium\",\"relevance\":\"high\"}\n{\"id\":\"R-f-حقق-صبر\",\"status\":\"reading\",\"finding\":\"40:77 directly grounds an imperative to be patient in God’s true promise, offering a truth-to-patience relation beside the focus’s ordered counsel of truth and patience; 2:61 supplies a contrasting refusal to endure.\",\"evidence\":[{\"ref\":\"40:77\",\"ar\":\"فَٱصْبِرْ إِنَّ وَعْدَ ٱللَّهِ حَقٌّۭ\"},{\"ref\":\"2:61\",\"ar\":\"لَن نَّصْبِرَ عَلَىٰ طَعَامٍۢ وَٰحِدٍۢ\"},{\"ref\":\"2:61\",\"ar\":\"وَيَقْتُلُونَ ٱلنَّبِيِّۦنَ بِغَيْرِ ٱلْحَقِّ\"},{\"ref\":\"103:3\",\"ar\":\"وَتَوَاصَوْا۟ بِٱلْحَقِّ وَتَوَاصَوْا۟ بِٱلصَّبْرِ\"}],\"activation\":\"The two focus payloads occur together in this family, and 40:77 explicitly places patience beside ḥaqq.\",\"limits\":\"40:77 is a singular command grounded in a divine promise, not mutual human counsel; 2:61 uses a verb of refusing patience in a separate episode.\",\"support\":\"strong\",\"relevance\":\"high\"}\n{\"id\":\"R-f-صبر-عمل\",\"status\":\"reading\",\"finding\":\"16:96 connects those who endured with reward measured by their deeds, while 52:16 says patience does not alter the punishment there; this makes the focus’s patience one condition alongside faith and action, not a substitute for them.\",\"evidence\":[{\"ref\":\"16:96\",\"ar\":\"وَلَنَجْزِيَنَّ ٱلَّذِينَ صَبَرُوٓا۟ أَجْرَهُم بِأَحْسَنِ مَا كَانُوا۟ يَعْمَلُونَ\"},{\"ref\":\"52:16\",\"ar\":\"فَٱصْلَوْهَا فَٱصْبِرُوٓا۟ أَوْ لَا تَصْبِرُوا۟ سَوَآءٌ عَلَيْكُمْ ۖ إِنَّمَا تُجْزَوْنَ مَا كُنتُمْ تَعْمَلُونَ\"},{\"ref\":\"103:3\",\"ar\":\"وَتَوَاصَوْا۟ بِٱلصَّبْرِ\"}],\"activation\":\"The focus coordinates belief and deeds before counsel of patience; the other passages distinguish patience’s relation to recompense across different settings.\",\"limits\":\"The forms differ: 16:96 has صَبَرُوا۟, 52:16 an imperative verb, and the focus’s بِٱلصَّبْرِ is the content of reciprocal counsel.\",\"support\":\"strong\",\"relevance\":\"high\"}\n{\"id\":\"R-f-حقق-صلح\",\"status\":\"open\",\"finding\":\"In 5:84, receiving truth and believing precedes the hope of being with the righteous; this may link the focus’s truth-counsel with its righteous-deed class.\",\"evidence\":[{\"ref\":\"5:84\",\"ar\":\"وَمَا جَآءَنَا مِنَ ٱلْحَقِّ\"},{\"ref\":\"5:84\",\"ar\":\"مَعَ ٱلْقَوْمِ ٱلصَّٰلِحِينَ\"},{\"ref\":\"103:3\",\"ar\":\"وَعَمِلُوا۟ ٱلصَّٰلِحَٰتِ\"},{\"ref\":\"103:3\",\"ar\":\"وَتَوَاصَوْا۟ بِٱلْحَقِّ\"}],\"missing\":\"The focus uses ٱلصَّٰلِحَٰتِ as deeds, while 5:84 describes a righteous people; a parallel showing how receiving or sharing truth leads to righteous action could establish the link between these forms.\",\"support\":\"medium\",\"relevance\":\"medium\"}\n{\"id\":\"R-f-عمل-وصي\",\"status\":\"reading\",\"finding\":\"The root و ص ي appears in 29:8 as God’s charge to a person concerning parents, while the focus uses the reciprocal form تَوَاصَوْا۟ for believers charging one another with truth and patience; the root’s direction shifts from divine instruction to mutual practice.\",\"evidence\":[{\"ref\":\"29:8\",\"ar\":\"وَوَصَّيْنَا ٱلْإِنسَٰنَ بِوَٰلِدَيْهِ حُسْنًۭا\"},{\"ref\":\"103:3\",\"ar\":\"وَتَوَاصَوْا۟ بِٱلْحَقِّ وَتَوَاصَوْا۟ بِٱلصَّبْرِ\"}],\"activation\":\"Both passages use forms of و ص ي for an ethical charge, but 29:8 has God as the giver and the focus has a plural reciprocal verb.\",\"limits\":\"The focus does not name parents or specify that its counsel concerns family obligations.\",\"support\":\"strong\",\"relevance\":\"high\"}"}}
